      "paragraph_type": "facts",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": 16,
      "chunk_id": "SC_2022_HEMANT_KUMAR_VERMA_VS_EMPLOYEES_STATE_INSURANCE_CORPORATI_P016_C01",
      "text": "have invoked the jurisdiction of this Court under\nArticle 32.\nThe petitioners’ have sought",
      "paragraph_type": "unknown",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": 17,
      "chunk_id": "SC_2022_HEMANT_KUMAR_VERMA_VS_EMPLOYEES_STATE_INSURANCE_CORPORATI_P017_C01",
      "text": "the following prayers:\n“(i) Issue a writ of Mandamus or any other appropriate Writ,\n order of direction to Respondents to declare that the\n Petitioners/Junior Resident Doctors are eligible “in-service”\n doctors of ESIC/ESIS for the purposes of inclusion in reservation\n for PG courses.\n(ii) Issue writ of mandamus or any other appropriate writ, order,\n direction to the Respondents to extend the 50% “in-service”\n doctors reservation for PG courses to the Junior Resident\n Doctors serving in ESIC/ESIS institutions.”\n3 The grievance of the petitioners is that that junior resident doctors and persons",
      "paragraph_type": "unknown",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": 18,
      "chunk_id": "SC_2022_HEMANT_KUMAR_VERMA_VS_EMPLOYEES_STATE_INSURANCE_CORPORATI_P018_C01",
      "text": "responsibilities. However, while reservation in postgraduate education is provided to the",
      "paragraph_type": "unknown",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
