      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": 23,
      "chunk_id": "SC_2022_HEMANT_KUMAR_VERMA_VS_EMPLOYEES_STATE_INSURANCE_CORPORATI_P023_C01",
      "text": "alia, contains the following stipulation:\n“2. The reduction in Bond duration and Bond amount would be\n prospective per-se, but in the following manner:",
      "paragraph_type": "unknown",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": 24,
      "chunk_id": "SC_2022_HEMANT_KUMAR_VERMA_VS_EMPLOYEES_STATE_INSURANCE_CORPORATI_P024_C01",
      "text": "2.1 The benefit of reduced Bond period & Bond amount in lieu, would\n also be extended to (i) all existing students (MBBS/BDS); (ii) Fresh\n UG (MBBS/BDS) pass-outs; and (ii) UG (MBBS/BDS) pass-outs\n already serving ESIC under Bond.\n2.2 In case of pass-outs already serving under Bond, if the length of\n service rendered is in excess of 01 year, they may be relieved\n without payment to ESIC for left over Bond period.”\n(iii) The petitioners completed their one year compulsory bond period",
      "paragraph_type": "unknown",
      "sections_cited": [],
      "cited_cases": [],
      "chunk_number": 1
    },
    {
